        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Understandable :slightly_smiling_face:.  \r\nThanks for pointing to #780 (_I also saw https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2087#issuecomment-3448190896 right after opening the PR_).\r\n\r\nFeels legit to want to keep 'mini.files'... minimal.  \r\nI'll see if I can achieve similar behavior without modifying 'mini.files' directly, possibly through the `MiniFilesWindowOpen` event (?).",
